@@ -26,19 +26,30 @@ BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 
 ## Working with Stripe
 
-The first time, you need to:
-
-1. Install Stripe CLI: https://stripe.com/docs/stripe-cli
-2. Run `stripe login` and authorize the environment `37signals Development`
-
-Then, for working on the Stripe integration locally, you need to run this script to start the tunneling and set the environment variables:
-
-```sh
-eval "$(BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle exec stripe-dev)"
-bin/dev # You need to start the dev server in the same terminal session
-```
-
-This will ask for your 1password authorization to read and set the environment variables that Stripe needs.
+Set these environment variables for the hosted app:
+
+| Variable | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` | The secret API key for this Stripe environment |
+| `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` | Recurring USD $20 monthly price for Unlimited |
+| `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID` | Recurring USD $25 monthly price for Unlimited+ |
+| `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Signing secret of the webhook endpoint (or local CLI listener) |
+
+In Stripe, enable the customer portal for these prices, including plan changes
+and cancellation. Enable Checkout's one-subscription-per-customer setting.
+Register `POST /stripe/webhooks` (no account prefix) for the snapshot events
+`customer.subscription.created`, `customer.subscription.updated`, and
+`customer.subscription.deleted`. The checkout return URL does not grant access:
+Fizzy verifies signed events and matches the Stripe customer to its local account.
+
+For local development with test prices, run `stripe listen --forward-to
+localhost:3000/stripe/webhooks` and use the signing secret it prints. The
+billing tests stub the Stripe API and sign webhook payloads locally.
+
+Run `bin/rails db:migrate:saas` before enabling billing on an existing hosted
+installation. Support staff can visit `/admin/accounts` to grant complimentary
+Unlimited access or override reported usage. These local controls do not edit
+Stripe subscriptions or the storage ledger. Reset restores measured usage.
 
 ### Stripe environments
 
